<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">New York Accords</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1988">1988</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Tripartite Accord (1988) · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-african-border-war">South African Border War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> Accords were signed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> on 22 December 1988 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angola">Angola</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>. They provided for the independence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namibia">Namibia</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations-security-council">United Nations Security Council</a> Resolution 435 and the phased withdrawal of Cuban troops from Angola. Namibia became independent in March 1990, ending South African rule and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-african-border-war">South African Border War</a>.</p></div>
